# Every environment variable this app reads. Copy to `.env.local` and fill in
# what you need — nothing here is required to run `pnpm dev`, and each feature
# degrades on its own rather than breaking the build.
#
# `.env.local` is gitignored. Set the same values on Vercel (Project →
# Settings → Environment Variables) or production will quietly run without
# them.

# --- Signups -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Klaviyo. Every form on the site that takes an address subscribes to one list
# and labels the consent record with the page it came from, so the pages stay
# separable inside a single audience.
#
# The key is a PRIVATE key (`pk_…`), created under Klaviyo → Settings → API
# keys, and it needs three scopes: lists:write, profiles:write,
# subscriptions:write. It is read in a server action and never reaches the
# browser, so it must NOT be prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_.
#
# The list id is the six-character code Klaviyo shows for the list — Lists &
# Segments → the list → Settings, or the tail of its URL.
#
# Unset in development, the form logs the address to the server console and
# answers as though it worked. Unset in production, it refuses the signup
# rather than dropping addresses silently.
KLAVIYO_API_KEY=
KLAVIYO_LIST_ID=

# --- Hero video --------------------------------------------------------------
# Mux playback ids. The backdrop is the looping hero footage; the feature is
# the film the "Watch 1.0 Aftermovie" bar opens.
#
# Both are optional and both fall back: the backdrop to `/hero-loop.mp4`, the
# feature to the aftermovie on YouTube. Public by design — a playback id is
# what the player fetches with.
NEXT_PUBLIC_MUX_BACKGROUND_PLAYBACK_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_MUX_HERO_PLAYBACK_ID=
